# Restora – Backend Overview

This repo is **Restora** (Restaurant Management System) **server only** (`RestaurentManagement-server`).
Do not edit `RestaurentManagement-client`. Do not put React or Next.js code here.

## Stack

- Node.js, Express, JavaScript (ES6+) only, MongoDB, Mongoose, Better Auth
- ESM (`"type": "module"`). Never add `.ts`, `.tsx`, or `tsconfig.json`
- Add Helmet, rate limiting, Zod, Socket.IO, or Cloudinary only when a feature needs them
- Do not install packages while only changing rules

## Boundaries

- Better Auth plus its MongoDB adapter owns identity, sessions, and credentials
- Mongoose owns application data. Do not store passwords in Mongoose
- Business rules, totals, and authorization run here. The UI is not a security boundary
- REST prefix `/api/v1`. Envelope: `{ success, data, message, error }`
- Work incrementally. Do not scaffold the whole app in one pass, and do not overwrite working code

## Roles

Backend source of truth: `admin`, `manager`, `waiter`, `chef`, `cashier`, `customer`.
The client rules still say `admin`, `staff`, `kitchen`, `customer`. Do not invent a third list, and do not change the client from this repo.

## Layout

```text
src/
├── config/
├── models/
├── routes/
├── controllers/
├── services/
├── middleware/
├── validators/
├── utils/
├── sockets/
├── auth/
├── app.js
└── server.js
```

Adapt to files that already exist. Create a folder only when the feature you are building needs it.
